    "description": "Every piece of data has a type. Today you learn the 3 most common types and how JavaScript handles them.",
    "type": "practice",
    "duration": 45,
    "steps": [
      "Open the console and try: typeof ''hello''",
      "Try: typeof 42 and typeof true",
      "Create a string: let greeting = ''Good morning, Alex!''",
      "Get its length: console.log(greeting.length)",
      "Convert a number to string: String(42)",
      "Convert a string to number: Number(''3.14'')",
      "Explore: what happens with typeof null? (this is a famous JavaScript quirk!)"
